Daniel Kraft wrote:

> I'm currently trying to ascend my first Samurai, and just won
> the Tsurugi; now I'm wondering whether I should use it as
> weapon or stick with my current configuration.

> At the moment I was twoweaponing Excalibur (got from a
> fountain) and a katana, which let monsters go down
> surprisingly fast.  Wielding the Tsurugi as two-handed sword
> does not allow twoweaponing any longer, and it seems to me it
> is weaker than Excalibur and the katana.

> What are your experiences/preferences as weapons for Samurai?
> I'd also like to hear what you usually use as weapon in the
> Endgame, I was thinking about twoweapon Grayswandir/Frostbrand
> or the like with katana/silver saber--any other
> recommendations or suggestions?

For practically any lawful, I'll be two weaponing Excalibur and
a long sword very early; I'll shift to a silver saber as the
second weapon for Gehemmon, and of course, use a Katana instead
of a long sword if I happen to have one.  I'll also replace
Excalibur with Grayswandir if I happen to get it, especially in
Gehemmon (but perhaps not before I've gotten magic
resistence---Excalibur makes searching for polymorph traps a lot
surer).

I don't think I've ever bothered with the Tsurugi.  (If you
couldn't twoweapon, it might be a different story.)

